    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** anchoring the lineup, both boasting elite efficiency scores as they capitalize on favorable matchups against Brown and Yarbrough, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our highest-projected asset (81.88) due to a prime leadoff spot and a 14% platoon edge, while **Kyle Tucker** (79.23) remains a must-start despite a minor dynamic platoon drag, primarily driven by his high base projection and the soft xERA profile of the opposing starter. **Andy Pages** (72.13) also warrants attention; he benefits from a rare combination of an elite SP skill matchup and a top-of-the-order designation, providing a significant boost in our target categories.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the exclusion of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (54.37), who fell just shy of our start threshold. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** offers high-end pedigree, the matchup against Burke and his relatively strong SP xERA (3.57) suppressed his efficiency enough to keep him on the bench in favor of more optimized, platoon-favored options like **Curtis Mead** (58.98) and **Nasim Nunez** (63.21). **Nasim Nunez** earns his place in the lineup primarily due to our ongoing organizational emphasis on stolen base potential; his speed remains a critical, albeit high-variance, asset in our pursuit of category gains.\n\nRegarding risk, we are closely monitoring the bottom of the order and our catching platoon. **Liam Hicks** (41.90) and **Heliot Ramos** (41.89) are currently operating near the \"below floor\" threshold; any shifts in batting order or confirmed lineup changes that further disadvantage these players could lead to late-day benching to preserve our game caps. While **Drake Baldwin** (48.70) remains our primary catcher start, his matchup against a high-caliber arm like Eovaldi necessitates a watchful eye on his actual performance in the first few innings. We are essentially betting on the volume of our leadoff-heavy hitters to outweigh the potential stagnation of our 5-hole occupants.",
